# Sentinel UI Style: Flight Recorder

Declared October 9, 2026 with the product direction change (see
`docs/Product Direction.md`). Replaces the September "cream canvas, blue
ticket" neobrutalist style, which read as a toy; a supervisor that keeps the
record of what agents did needs to read as an instrument. References the user
chose: the *Impact* card (one orange column carrying the only number that
matters, hairline grid, mono labels), the *Aetheron* posters (ink and orange,
mono uppercase headings, texture that means something), and the *District 9*
operations page (paper floor, one dense orange data panel, technical drawing,
release markers).

This is the project-declared style under Owen's `my-ui-standard` skill; that
skill's composition principles (emphasis budget, layout follows the job,
alignment is the design, no bento) still apply and win over anything here.

**Timing.** The old pages (Tasks form, proposal card, budget UI) are being
retired, and the new pages (Monitor, Flight recorder) have no backend until
Weeks 16-17. Do not restyle the old pages. Apply this rule to new surfaces as
their data arrives; migrate shared primitives (`layout.tsx`, `ticket.tsx`)
when the first new page is built, not before.

## Tokens

```css
--paper: #f4f4f2;        /* page floor */
--panel: #ffffff;        /* panels and table surfaces */
--line: #dcdcd8;         /* hairlines, 1px */
--line-strong: #121212;  /* 1.5px structure: sidebar edge, header edge */
--ink: #121212;
--subtext: #5c5c5a;
--faint: #8a8a86;        /* eyebrows, placeholders; check ≥4.5:1 at 11px */
--attention: #f04e12;    /* the one orange; see "verdict colours" */
--attention-ink: #121212;/* text on orange is ink, never white */
--hatch: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, transparent 0 4px, #121212 4px 5px);
--radius-control: 6px;
--radius-panel: 8px;
--font-sans: Inter or Geist Sans, 13-14px body;
--font-mono: Geist Mono, tabular-nums, for every fact;
```

No dark mode in the app. Black-on-orange (Aetheron) is reserved for marketing
and poster surfaces, not tool chrome.

## Orange is attention, not decoration

- **One orange block per screen, and only when something needs the person.**
  A pending confirm, a stuck signal, a widening question, an active boundary
  the person just answered. A quiet session is a gray screen with nothing
  orange on it. The emphasis budget becomes product behaviour: silence looks
  like silence.
- The orange block is a solid fill with ink text and ink hairlines inside it
  (Impact's column, District 9's panel). It is never a tint, a badge, an icon
  tile, or an eyebrow. Never two orange regions; never orange plus a raised
  button elsewhere.
- **Verdict colours map to tiers, nothing else:**
  - `allow` and routine: ink on paper, no colour.
  - `warn` and `confirm_required`: the orange block.
  - `block`: a solid ink fill with paper text. Ink plus orange reads as
    severe; there is no red in the palette.
  - Status dots stay 6px: ink for live, `--faint` for idle, hatched for
    advisory. No green.

## Texture carries meaning

- **Diagonal hatching (`--hatch`) means "advisory or unverified."** Used on
  coverage cells where Sentinel can only observe, on a host row whose hook
  file the agent can edit, on a ceiling that has not been verified against the
  state database. Solid fill means enforced. Nothing is hatched for looks.
- **Dithered orange imagery** (Aetheron) is for the marketing site and for the
  app's few empty states, drawn, never real screenshots. It does not appear
  in chrome, headers, or panels.
- **The technical drawing** (District 9) is the coverage map: one exploded
  diagram of an agent with shell, files, MCP, browser, and hooks labelled,
  hatched where advisory. Drawn once as SVG; not a chart library.

## Type and facts

- Five sizes: 10.5-11px eyebrow (mono, uppercase, +0.08em, `--faint`), 12px
  meta, 13px body, 14px emphasis, 28px display for the one statement of
  current state (−0.02em). Weights 400/500/600.
- **Every fact is mono, label-first, lower case:** `host: claude-code`,
  `boundary: ~/repo · dev`, `ceiling: v2 · a81f3c`, `hooks: managed · locked`.
  Version and count markers follow District 9: `release 5.1 · 203/234`.
- Numbers right-aligned, tabular, in mono. Times absolute (`07:28:04`), not
  relative, because this is a record.
- Icons: Lucide, 15px, stroke 1.5, only where they earn a place. No icon per
  row.

## Structure

- Paper floor, white panels, 1px `--line` hairlines inside, 1.5px
  `--line-strong` for the sidebar and header edges only. No shadows anywhere,
  no offset shadows, no notches, no rounded "tickets."
- Panels are for genuinely separate objects (a log, a form, a dialog). Page
  structure is typography, whitespace, and hairlines. Tables are framed by
  hairlines, never boxed, and are the truth for history.
- Buttons: primary is solid ink with paper text; secondary is a 1px ink
  outline; a destructive confirm is primary (ink), never orange, because
  orange is the *question*, ink is the *answer*.
- Motion: one moment only, when a verdict needs the person: the orange block
  paints in left to right over 180ms. Nothing else animates. Respect
  `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Composition by page (new product)

- **Monitor** (replaces Overview): hero statement + ledger. One line of
  current state in 28px (`Claude Code · working in ~/repo · 42 actions, 0
  interruptions`), under it the boundary as mono facts, then a hairline
  ledger of recent verdicts: time, host, action, verdict, reason. If a verdict
  needs the person, the ledger row is the orange block and the hero line names
  it. No enforcement grid of cards; coverage lives on its own page.
- **Flight recorder** (replaces Activity): the District 9 panel. One dense
  mono table filling the viewport, filterable by host, boundary, verdict,
  rule; every row carries its chain position (`#2041 · prev a8f1`); a deleted
  or edited row shows as a hatched gap with the break named. The table scrolls
  inside; the filter bar is pinned.
- **Approvals**: document page. One pending confirm at a time as the orange
  block: the exact canonical action in mono, the floor rule that fired, the
  working directory, the TTL counting down in mono, and one ink primary
  ("Allow this exact action") beside a secondary ("Deny"). Nothing else on the
  page.
- **Coverage**: the technical drawing, with a hairline table under it: host,
  surface, mandatory / advisory / unsupported, why, hook hash.
- **Settings**: grouped sections, left nav, hairline rows in one white panel
  per group. The ceiling version and hash shown as facts, read-only.
- Retired from the primary flow: Tasks form, proposal card, budget controls,
  the ticket. Keep the fixture bench reachable from Settings if the Week 15
  delete-or-bench decision keeps it; do not restyle it.

## Primitives to build when the first new page lands

`Statement` (the 28px hero line), `Facts` (mono label-first list),
`Ledger` (hairline table with pinned header and internal scroll),
`Attention` (the orange block, ink text, left-to-right paint),
`Hatch` (advisory fill), `Eyebrow`. Replace `Ticket`, `TicketFacts`, `Chip`,
and the raised `Button` variant; keep `Panel`, `SectionHeader`,
`KeyValueList` with the new tokens.

